cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use paperlab-space in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "paperlab-space: no-code LLM evaluation on spreadsheet data"
abstract: >-
  paperlab-space is the open-source engine behind PaperLab.space. It evaluates large
  language models on researchers' own Excel or CSV data and produces paper-ready
  results: per-row outputs and scores in Excel, a LaTeX comparison table, and a
  reproducibility config recording model versions, prompts, seeds, metric settings,
  and a hash of the data. It supports many providers through LiteLLM, rate-limit-aware
  runs with retries and resume, and metrics that handle non-Latin scripts such as
  Burmese, Thai, Chinese, and Japanese.
type: software
authors:
  # Full name kept as one string (Burmese names have no family-name part).
  - family-names: "Kaung Nay Lin Khant"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-5612-5755"
# Concept DOI: always resolves to the latest version. Each release also gets its own DOI on Zenodo.
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23436738
repository-code: "https://github.com/paperlab-space/paperlab-core"
url: "https://paperlab.space"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.2
date-released: 2026-10-17
keywords:
  - large language models
  - evaluation
  - reproducibility
  - multilingual
